into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {3}^{2} & =4p(6) \\\\ 9 & =24p \\\\ p & =\\frac{3}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4(\\frac{3}{8})x \\\\ {y}^{2} & =\\frac{3}{2}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186310780 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "17099881-d7b9-54d9-a29a-4f5f28561cd3" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Left or Right-Opening Parabola with Vertex at the Origin Given Another Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "222fe8d9-adb9-5edd-9390-b3f17d688162" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}=4x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310782} {:answer/id #uuid "4fb7c43c-4396-5b6d-93e9-c2fec148eaa8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}=2y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310783} {:answer/id #uuid "d27b95c3-9e3e-5631-9fc6-c218385ff2ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}=-\\frac{1}{2}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310784} {:answer/id #uuid "77218e5c-a3c9-5d7e-bd57-a4edc28c8df4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}=-2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310785} {:answer/id #uuid "8f6380dc-ec5b-526c-b610-b79baf1aca19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}=-\\frac{1}{2}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310786}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "77218e5c-a3c9-5d7e-bd57-a4edc28c8df4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}=-2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310785} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f30297e-01ec-5ead-8058-5f9754035dfa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310781}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b24732f9-7b75-59b2-a18e-ce5ccd87f7dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-115633" :question/problem "Find the equation of the left-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(0,0)$ and passes through the point $(-2,-2).$" :question/worked-solution "The general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(0,0)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSince we know the given parabola passes through the point $(-2,-2),$ we can substitute $x=-2$ and $y=-2$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ (-2)^{2} & =4p(-2) \\\\ 4 & =-8p \\\\ p & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4(-\\frac{1}{2})x \\\\ {y}^{2} & =-2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266687 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dc86c375-c2c4-56b7-a207-0abfc9709f6a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Left or Right-Opening Parabola Given a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a282ecd-9120-5164-9142-e8fed956f6fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(y-3)^{2}=-\\frac{3}{8}(x-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266689} {:answer/id #uuid "01480733-3dea-5b7a-a998-8e6987364ac0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(y+3)^{2}=3(x+3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266690} {:answer/id #uuid "90da7ecc-92e5-566f-b1ae-aa71cd79d6d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(y+3)^{2}=\\frac{3}{2}(x+3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266691} {:answer/id #uuid "6faf3cff-1208-501c-bd13-4ddc53d72dba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-3)^{2}=-12(y-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266692} {:answer/id #uuid "3a407151-85b6-55e5-94c1-77ac3be02ee1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(y-3)^{2}=12(x-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266693}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3a407151-85b6-55e5-94c1-77ac3be02ee1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(y-3)^{2}=12(x-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266693} :answer-field/id #uuid "094bad5d-3056-51a0-b6a9-d51a378c2415" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266688}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a7d690cd-8b12-547d-a0c5-09b9dbca554a" :question/math-academy-id "q-115640" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041337/assets/c88e54f2a7acec3815a53fa4b0d641dd370ccf708b876f8dd231f05e115ea6fc.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the parabola shown above?" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram we see that the arms of the parabola open to the right. The parabola has its vertex at $(3,3)$ and passes through the point $(6,-3).$\n\nThe general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(h,k)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-k)^{2} & =4p(x-h).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we know that the given parabola has its vertex at $(h,k)=(3,3),$ we substitute $h=3$ and $k=3$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-3)^{2} & =4p(x-3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also know that the given parabola passes through the point $(6,-3),$ so we can substitute $x=6$ and $y=-3$ into the equation above and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-3)^{2} & =4p(x-3) \\\\ (-3-3)^{2} & =4p(6-3) \\\\ 36 & =12p \\\\ p & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-3)^{2} & =4p(x-3) \\\\ (y-3)^{2} & =4(3)(x-3) \\\\ (y-3)^{2} & =12(x-3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the arms of the parabola open to the right since $p=3$ is positive."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275593 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "783ca59b-0242-584c-ae47-004a0eb03817" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Left or Right-Opening Parabola Given the Vertex and Another Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b544aef-4b08-566e-b89f-6375a971585d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}=\\frac{9}{5}(x-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275595} {:answer/id #uuid "4c76720f-5fc0-51b7-81e1-07a6b885a8a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(y+2)^{2}=\\frac{9}{20}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275596} {:answer/id #uuid "aed3fca7-d8d1-57a1-b538-8ed46c92bfa6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}=\\frac{9}{5}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275597} {:answer/id #uuid "b019f271-7470-5ee4-bd93-d25a46cebb3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}=\\frac{9}{20}y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275598} {:answer/id #uuid "024188a7-1314-5685-a589-3841147df8e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(y-2)^{2}=\\frac{9}{5}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275599}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "024188a7-1314-5685-a589-3841147df8e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(y-2)^{2}=\\frac{9}{5}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275599} :answer-field/id #uuid "f922b8c4-d133-5566-9064-c0537c542bff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275594}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0695a7e0-e42c-5754-8590-aebc60ec68a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-115648" :question/problem "Find the equation of the right-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(0,2)$ and passes through the point $(5,5).$" :question/worked-solution "The general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(h,k)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-k)^{2} & =4p(x-h).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we know that the given parabola has its vertex at $(h,k)=(0,2),$ we substitute $h=0$ and $k=2$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-2)^{2} & =4px.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also know that the given parabola passes through the point $(5,5),$ so we can substitute $x=5$ and $y=5$ into the equation above and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-2)^{2} & =4px \\\\ (5-2)^{2} & =4p(5) \\\\ 9 & =20p \\\\ p & =\\frac{9}{20}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-2)^{2} & =4px \\\\ (y-2)^{2} & =4(\\frac{9}{20})x \\\\ (y-2)^{2} & =\\frac{9}{5}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311499 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "75fd35db-6b4e-5820-b6ac-925d24a0f117" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Left or Right-Opening Parabola with Vertex at the Origin Given a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26a0af48-afbe-5a03-bcd1-4c94ec5d4e7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}=4x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311501} {:answer/id #uuid "3cc2b354-e19b-5b69-b8c3-1f46f5f0da8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}=2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311502} {:answer/id #uuid "a2eba45d-9fa2-54c1-aa3f-6cf10c2beb51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}=-8x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311503} {:answer/id #uuid "9ffc591d-10ab-59a2-aae6-4cf077e4f94d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}=8x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311504} {:answer/id #uuid "17669a5a-57fe-539c-bffd-87a4fe3b023e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}=-2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311505}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9ffc591d-10ab-59a2-aae6-4cf077e4f94d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}=8x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311504} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba363e23-37f7-59d9-99d5-05731f83c2c2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311500}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9763dfd0-41fb-5dba-b188-a16eaef5f08a" :question/math-academy-id "q-11750" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041337/assets/b2caf9c9ff75af69d9de7bd1409317229b5d34adf2c64464cd2af2229af0476b.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the parabola shown above?" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram we see that the arms of the parabola open to the right. The parabola has its vertex at $(0,0)$ and passes through the point $(8,8).$\n\nThe general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(0,0)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSince we know the given parabola passes through the point $(8,8),$ we can substitute $x=8$ and $y=8$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {8}^{2} & =4p(8) \\\\ 64 & =32p \\\\ p & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4(2)x \\\\ {y}^{2} & =8x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the arms of the parabola open to the right since $p=2$ is positive."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266715 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "17099881-d7b9-54d9-a29a-4f5f28561cd3" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Left or Right-Opening Parabola with Vertex at the Origin Given Another Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "edb3077d-eeda-5dc3-b79c-f796b335c13e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}=-8x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266717} {:answer/id #uuid "75105eb6-7716-5a06-9451-922804cb471e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}=6x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266718} {:answer/id #uuid "c641f368-a0eb-5fa6-a43a-b2f490b47a3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{y}^{2}=8x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266719} {:answer/id #uuid "20710e9e-58c5-5498-a5ba-a5e4cafe2e28" :answer/type 